<%# The cross-links under every auth screen ("Log in", "Sign up", "Forgot your
    password?"). Each branch is Devise's own guard on the mapping and the current
    controller, and the link text is frozen product copy.

    HOOJAH 2026 (Phase 1.1) — restyled into the mockup's footer strip: a single
    hairline-topped row, centered, muted body text with a bold primary-coloured
    call-to-action span, replacing the plain bulleted-link stack from Slice 9.

    The recoverable branch below now ALSO excludes `sessions`, which it didn't
    before this restyle: "Forgot password?" moved onto the log-in screen itself,
    inline under the primary submit button (see devise/sessions/new, matching the
    mockup). Rendering it again down here would duplicate the link. passwords/
    registrations were already excluded (a screen doesn't link to itself).

    This app is neither confirmable nor lockable and has no omniauth providers, so
    the last three branches never render today. They are Devise's, they cost
    nothing, and deleting them would silently drop the links if a module is ever
    switched on — left unstyled since there is no mockup for them to match.
%>
<div class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-hairline text-center text-[13.5px] text-ink-2">
  <%- if controller_name != 'sessions' %>
    <p>Already have an account? <%= link_to "Log in", new_session_path(resource_name), class: "text-primary font-bold" %></p>
  <% end %>

  <%- if devise_mapping.registerable? && controller_name != 'registrations' %>
    <p>New here? <%= link_to "Sign up", new_registration_path(resource_name), class: "text-primary font-bold" %></p>
  <% end %>

  <%- if devise_mapping.recoverable? && controller_name != 'passwords' && controller_name != 'registrations' && controller_name != 'sessions' %>
    <p><%= link_to "Forgot your password?", new_password_path(resource_name) %></p>
  <% end %>

  <%- if devise_mapping.confirmable? && controller_name != 'confirmations' %>
    <p><%= link_to "Didn't receive confirmation instructions?", new_confirmation_path(resource_name) %></p>
  <% end %>

  <%- if devise_mapping.lockable? && resource_class.unlock_strategy_enabled?(:email) && controller_name != 'unlocks' %>
    <p><%= link_to "Didn't receive unlock instructions?", new_unlock_path(resource_name) %></p>
  <% end %>

  <%- if devise_mapping.omniauthable? %>
    <%- resource_class.omniauth_providers.each do |provider| %>
      <p><%= button_to "Sign in with #{OmniAuth::Utils.camelize(provider)}", omniauth_authorize_path(resource_name, provider), data: { turbo: false } %></p>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
